# OSS-Phone-V1 stage-2 containment relay.
#
# Appended to init.rc by magiskinit and run by the CONTAINED Android init
# (inside its PID + mount namespace). It talks to the host PID 1 (oss-init)
# through the shared /oss-run tmpfs oss-init mounted before cloning:
#
#   /oss-run/alive     written as soon as the container's init runs, so the
#                      host can tell a healthy (if slow) boot from a wedged one
#                      and only break a genuine early hang.
#   /oss-run/powerctl  the reboot/shutdown request, so the host can perform the
#                      real power transition (reboot(2) from a child PID
#                      namespace only tears the namespace down).
#
# If /oss-run is absent (relay disabled, e.g. mount failed on the host) these
# writes are harmless no-ops and the host degrades to the safe default: a
# container death becomes a fresh uncontained boot.

on early-init
    write /oss-run/alive 1

on property:sys.powerctl=*
    write /oss-run/powerctl ${sys.powerctl}
